WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.310
(uplifting electronic music)

00:00:04.310 --> 00:00:06.210
- Being trans is not that hard.

00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:09.580
It's being trans in a world
that doesn't like trans people;

00:00:09.580 --> 00:00:10.413
that is hard.

00:00:10.413 --> 00:00:12.110
Transphobia's hard.

00:00:12.110 --> 00:00:13.990
We're such a small community.

00:00:13.990 --> 00:00:16.120
We can't fight this battle ourselves.

00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:18.530
When I do people's
nails, it's about hoping

00:00:18.530 --> 00:00:20.320
that people go away with
more than a manicure.

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:21.663
They go away an ally.

00:00:30.908 --> 00:00:33.210
(inspirational electronic music)

00:00:33.210 --> 00:00:36.010
I'm Charlie Craggs, and I'm
a trans activist and author.

00:00:37.957 --> 00:00:39.720
Nail Transphobia is a campaign I run

00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:42.560
where I travel around the
UK with a popup nail salon,

00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:44.390
and I offer the public free nails for

00:00:44.390 --> 00:00:46.920
the chance to sit down and have
a chat with a trans person.

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:48.770
When people sit down and
get their nails done by me,

00:00:48.770 --> 00:00:52.173
that's my way of showing that
trans people are just human.

00:00:54.270 --> 00:00:56.070
As a child, I knew that I was different,

00:00:56.070 --> 00:00:57.980
and I knew that I felt like a girl.

00:00:57.980 --> 00:01:00.290
I really tried to repress it, and I was

00:01:00.290 --> 00:01:02.760
so angry at myself for being feminine.

00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:04.180
I wanted to be like the boys in school

00:01:04.180 --> 00:01:05.913
so I wouldn't be bullied anymore.

00:01:07.330 --> 00:01:09.800
I'm Irish, working-class Catholic.

00:01:09.800 --> 00:01:11.630
I had a lot of cards stacked against me,

00:01:11.630 --> 00:01:14.187
and I was like, "It might
be hard transitioning,

00:01:14.187 --> 00:01:16.567
"but I'm gonna kill myself if I don't."

00:01:17.549 --> 00:01:19.290
(mournful music)

00:01:19.290 --> 00:01:22.230
My life became a lot, lot
harder when I came out as trans

00:01:22.230 --> 00:01:24.560
in a way I didn't even anticipate.

00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:27.160
In my early transition, after a night out,

00:01:27.160 --> 00:01:29.360
I was at a park bus stop.

00:01:29.360 --> 00:01:30.620
These guys came over.

00:01:30.620 --> 00:01:32.040
I saw one of them look at me.

00:01:32.040 --> 00:01:33.290
He was like trying to flirt with me.

00:01:33.290 --> 00:01:35.330
I could tell he didn't
realize I was trans,

00:01:35.330 --> 00:01:36.747
and then he was like, "Oh, my god.

00:01:36.747 --> 00:01:37.710
"That's a man."

00:01:37.710 --> 00:01:39.710
He grabbed my boobs, and then it kind

00:01:39.710 --> 00:01:41.210
of became a bit more physical.

00:01:43.160 --> 00:01:44.840
After it was done, I'm a mess.

00:01:44.840 --> 00:01:46.890
No one came over and asked me, "Am I OK?"

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:48.940
No one looked at me.

00:01:48.940 --> 00:01:50.940
I was dirt, and that, I don't wanna cry.

00:01:51.790 --> 00:01:53.580
But that's like-- (exhales)

00:01:53.580 --> 00:01:57.980
It just really showed me
like what people think of me.

00:01:57.980 --> 00:02:00.530
It really, really hurt that
no one asked if I was OK.

00:02:00.530 --> 00:02:03.370
I just realized, I was
like, "We need allies,"

00:02:03.370 --> 00:02:05.100
not just in the fight for our rights,

00:02:05.100 --> 00:02:07.163
but the fight that's our everyday lives.

00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:16.820
When I started the
campaign five years ago,

00:02:16.820 --> 00:02:18.197
I was like, "Why is no one aware

00:02:18.197 --> 00:02:19.377
"of how hard it is to be trans,

00:02:19.377 --> 00:02:20.947
"how much abuse I'm getting and the fact

00:02:20.947 --> 00:02:22.477
"that, when I transitioned, my chance

00:02:22.477 --> 00:02:25.470
"of being murdered went up to one in 12?"

00:02:25.470 --> 00:02:27.310
What I do with Nail Transphobia is

00:02:27.310 --> 00:02:28.830
about humanizing an issue.

00:02:28.830 --> 00:02:31.570
I hire other trans people
to come do nails with me.

00:02:31.570 --> 00:02:34.470
You're getting different stories
and different narratives.

00:02:35.360 --> 00:02:36.490
It's about sitting down, one-on-one,

00:02:36.490 --> 00:02:38.600
person-to-person, holding hands.

00:02:38.600 --> 00:02:40.670
You can't get more human.

00:02:40.670 --> 00:02:43.400
If I was to sit there with
a table full of brochures

00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:46.090
about trans people,
they're not gonna interact,

00:02:46.090 --> 00:02:48.960
whereas if I'm offering nails,
people love a free manicure.

00:02:48.960 --> 00:02:50.563
People are gonna be interested.

00:02:51.520 --> 00:02:53.450
I want to reach that straight boy

00:02:53.450 --> 00:02:55.090
who has never met a trans person,

00:02:55.090 --> 00:02:56.550
or even an LGBT person, before.

00:02:56.550 --> 00:02:58.870
I wanna reach the old
lady who doesn't even know

00:02:58.870 --> 00:03:00.830
what LGBT means, so that, if they're

00:03:00.830 --> 00:03:02.210
out and the see someone being attacked,

00:03:02.210 --> 00:03:03.380
they might say something, 'cause then

00:03:03.380 --> 00:03:04.880
they have that emotional link.

00:03:06.170 --> 00:03:09.120
Most times people will
ask the wrong question,

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:12.230
but it's the perfect time
to ask that wrong question.

00:03:12.230 --> 00:03:13.973
I'll be like, "Oh, babes,
we don't ask that yet."

00:03:13.973 --> 00:03:14.806
Well, I'll have to explain why,

00:03:14.806 --> 00:03:17.820
but I explain in a nice
way, in an accessible way.

00:03:17.820 --> 00:03:19.990
I've done probably 10,000 conversations,

00:03:19.990 --> 00:03:21.910
and to know that like they're on-side now.

00:03:21.910 --> 00:03:23.290
They go away, and they love me.

00:03:23.290 --> 00:03:24.540
They're like, "Oh, you've really changed

00:03:24.540 --> 00:03:25.373
"my mind about this."

00:03:25.373 --> 00:03:26.580
And to think that they will now raise

00:03:26.580 --> 00:03:30.593
their kids to be decent,
non-transphobic people.

00:03:31.880 --> 00:03:34.800
That's so exciting to me,
knowing that ripples make waves,

00:03:34.800 --> 00:03:36.530
and you've put an ally out into the world,

00:03:36.530 --> 00:03:38.513
and allies make other allies.

00:03:42.310 --> 00:03:44.640
It really makes me happy to know

00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:47.040
that trans people won't have to

00:03:47.040 --> 00:03:50.010
all go through the same
thing that I went through.

00:03:50.010 --> 00:03:51.690
I took the negative and I turned

00:03:51.690 --> 00:03:53.300
it into something positive, and I feel

00:03:53.300 --> 00:03:57.650
like that is often the only
way to get through life.

00:03:57.650 --> 00:03:59.530
I'm very proud to be trans.

00:03:59.530 --> 00:04:00.458
Someone's gotta be.

00:04:00.458 --> 00:04:03.958
(classy electronic music)

